			(property "Description" "Cold-Junction-Compensated K-Thermocoupleto-Digital Converter (-270°C to +1800°C) The MAX31855K performs cold-junction compensation and digitizes the signal from a type-K thermocouple. The data is output in a 14-bit resolution, SPI™-compatible, read-only format. This converter resolves temperatures to 0.25°C, allows readings as high as +1800°C and as low as -270°C, and exhibits thermocouple accuracy of ±2°C for temperatures ranging from -200°C to +700°C for K-type thermocouples."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
